<title>UK: Anglian to make provision, cut jobs.</title>
<headline>Anglian to make provision, cut jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British water company Anglian Water Plc said on Wednesday that it will make a provision of 20 million pounds to cover a reduction of up to 300 jobs.</p>
<p>It expects its review to improve the performance of the business and give savings of around 10 million pounds per annum.  </p>
<p>Anglian said the provision will be made in the 1996/97 accounts and that the job reductions will be in the production and networks divisions of Anglian Water Services Ltd.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the majority of the redundancies will be voluntary, although it could not rule out some compulsory redundancies.</p>
</text>
